Package: DspikeIn
Type: Package
Title: Estimating Absolute Abundance from Microbial Spike-in Controls
Version: 1.2.3
Authors@R: 
    person(given = "Mitra", family = "Ghotbi", role = c("aut", "cre"), 
           email = "mitra.ghotbi@gmail.com")
Maintainer: Mitra Ghotbi <mitra.ghotbi@gmail.com>
Description: 
    DspikeIn provides tools to estimate absolute microbial abundance using spike-in 
    controls, supporting the analysis of microbial dynamics — a key aspect of 
    microbial ecology. The package builds on the phyloseq framework and integrates 
    functionality from several established packages, including dplyr, stats, 
    ggplot2, edgeR, DESeq2, microbiome, microbiomeutilities, DECIPHER, speedyseq, 
    and ggtree. It enables data integration, differential abundance analysis, and 
    advanced visualization, leveraging Bioconductor infrastructure such as 
    TreeSummarizedExperiment.
Acknowledgment: 
    This package makes use of public APIs from several R packages including phyloseq, 
    microbiome, microbiomeutilities, speedyseq, ggtree, edgeR, DESeq2, and ggplot2 
    for analysis and visualization. We thank the authors of these tools for their 
    contributions to the R and Bioconductor ecosystem.
